add(SECTIONS, 213, 'OCP consumption, regimens and missed-pill source algorithm', '''
fillup | OCPs can be started at any time if appropriate, but the ideal cycle-day window given is ____. | Days 1–5 | Days 7–10 | Days 12–14 | Days 21–26 | The method-of-consumption box gives D1–D5 as ideal; pregnancy exclusion is important for other starts.
fillup | Starting OCPs after day 5 requires backup for ____ in the source. | 7 days | 48 hours | 24 hours | 3 months | This is separate from the 48-hour backup period later used for delayed POPs.
fillup | Routine OCP use is one pill ____ at ____. | Daily; the same time | Weekly; any time | On alternate days; bedtime only | Monthly; ovulation | The daily same-time instruction supports consistent adherence.
fillup | A 28-tablet pack in this example contains ____ hormonal tablets plus ____ tablets of ____. | 21; 7; ferrous fumarate | 24; 4; levonorgestrel only | 7; 21; ethinyl estradiol | 14; 14; clomiphene | The source's example is a 21-active/7-iron pack, not every 28-tablet product.
scenario | In the source's 28-tablet example, what should happen despite menstruation occurring? | Start the fresh pack as scheduled | Stop pills until bleeding has ceased for a month | Restart only after a positive LH kit | Take iron tablets indefinitely instead of active pills | The pack instruction continues into a fresh pack; bleeding should not create an extra hormone-free gap.
fillup | In the 21-tablet example, the routine pattern is ____. | One daily for 3 weeks, then 1 week off | One daily for 1 week, then 3 weeks off | Two daily for 21 days, then 14 days off | Only on days with intercourse | The source describes three weeks of pills and one week off.
scenario | The 21-tablet box also says to start the next pack on the first menstrual day. What is the key safety clarification? | Do not extend the scheduled hormone-free interval while waiting for bleeding | Always wait for a full extra week after menstruation | Menstruation is required to prove tubal patency | Bleeding cancels the need for all future pills | The source wording is ambiguous; a new pack follows the product schedule rather than an unpredictable bleed.
match | Match regimens: 1) 21/7 2) 24/4 with A) 24 hormonal days plus 4 off B) 21 hormonal days plus 7 off. | 1-B, 2-A | 1-A, 2-B | Both A | Both B | The numbers represent hormonal exposure and the hormone-free interval in each source regimen.
fillup | The notes attribute ____ efficacy and ____ side effects to the 24/4 regimen. | Better; fewer | Worse; more | Equal; universally absent | Lower; irreversible | These are the two arrows beneath 24/4; they are the source's comparison rather than a guarantee for every formulation.
fillup | Multiphasic pills contain ____ and are labelled ____ in this source. | Different doses within one pack; obsolete | Identical doses in every pill; most preferred | Only iron tablets; permanent | No hormones; emergency-only | The source uses the label obsolete; multiphasic products still exist, so that label is not a universal availability claim.
fillup | Post-pill amenorrhoea is attributed in the diagram to endometrial thinning by ____. | Progesterone/progestin | TSH | Inhibin B | hCG | The source diagram distinguishes delayed bleeding from permanent loss of fertility.
fillup | Return of fertility after stopping OCPs is described as rapid, within ____. | 3 months | 12–18 months | 2 years | 5 years | This contrasts with the longer delay described for DMPA.
scenario | Under the page's 'missed 1 or 2 pills' line, what action is stated? | Take one ASAP or two at the scheduled time; no backup is listed | Take one ASAP, add seven days of backup, then take a seven-day break | Omit the missed dose, finish the pack, and use backup for forty-eight hours | Take two daily until the pack ends, adding a seven-day hormone-free interval | This tests the printed source algorithm, not a universal current missed-pill instruction.
scenario | The next source heading says 'missed ≥2 pills', overlapping the '1 or 2' line. What should the learner recognise? | The exact-two-pill case is internally inconsistent and needs product/current-guideline advice | Both contradictory lines can be followed simultaneously | Two missed pills never matter for any product | Only ferrous fumarate can restore ovulation suppression | The overlapping headings must be flagged rather than choosing an unsafe unqualified instruction.
fillup | Under the source's missed-≥2-pill pathway, backup is advised for ____. | 7 days | 48 hours | 1 hour | 6 months | The seven-day backup instruction appears in the general branch and again under week 1/2.
fillup | The missed-pill branch names emergency contraception when unprotected intercourse occurred in the previous ____. | 72 hours | 7 minutes | 14 days | 3 months | This is the source's specified interval; current emergency-method windows and indications are method-dependent.
scenario | In source weeks 1–2 after multiple missed pills, which pack action is written? | Take one immediately and complete the pack on schedule | Discard all active tablets and wait for menstruation | Double every future daily dose indefinitely | Take only iron tablets for the rest of the month | The action is immediate replacement plus continuing the pack, with backup and EC assessment as stated.
scenario | In source week 3 after multiple missed pills, how is the hormone-free gap handled? | Finish active pills and immediately start the next pack, omitting non-hormonal pills | Add an extra seven pill-free days | Take iron tablets for two consecutive weeks | Wait for a positive pregnancy test before resuming | The week-3 branch avoids an extended hormone-free interval.
tf | I) The missed-pill source algorithm varies by week of the pack. II) It advises an extra pill-free week after missed pills in week 3. | I true; II false | I false; II true | Both true | Both false | Week 3 specifically calls for a new pack without the non-hormonal gap.
''')
